message:
refactor(ui): split our own components out of the base design system

@repo/ui was two things at once: the base layer (gruvbox tokens, the
shadcn primitives, the vendored ai-elements, fonts, styles) and the
components we wrote on top of it. The second kind now lives in
@repo/components, which depends on @repo/ui, so the base package depends
on no workspace package at all.

The vote's survey contract and its quips came along, out of
@repo/shared and into feedback.ts beside the component that is their
only caller. @repo/shared goes back to holding what two packages both
need and neither owns, and @repo/ui no longer depends on it.

@repo/ui keeps no tests of its own, so its vitest config goes with them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
